      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFixes #60109: HiSparse servers crash with an illegal memory access when a new request hits a prefix whose published host pages still have GPU copies.\n\nThe coordinator adopts those copies after the scheduler has already built the request's `NewRequestData`, so the adopted row went out as a `block_table_updates` entry. For a new request, model runner V2 then stages two full-row writes for the same row in one step (`add_requests`, then `update_requests`), and the staged-write kernel applies them in parallel with no ordering. A rank that kept the pre-adoption row saw null resident pages, while the scheduler reported every context page resident. The resident-prefill shortcut then sent the prefill rows through the decode residency resolver, whose host union overflowed `max_union_rows` and faulted.\n\nThe fix puts the adopted row in the new request's `block_ids`; `block_table_updates` stays for running requests. HiSparse-only (`hisparse/connector.py`).\n\nNote: MRv2's staged block-table writer doesn't order overlapping writes to the same row. This PR stops HiSparse from producing them; changing that in core is a separate discussion.\n\n## Reproduction on main\n\nGLM-5.3-NVFP4 on B200, either TP8 or TP4 (`host_pool_gib` 128 or 64):\n\n```bash\nvllm serve RedHatAI/GLM-5.3-NVFP4 -tp 4 --kv-cache-dtype fp8 --block-size 64 \\\n  --max-model-len 22528 --max-num-seqs 256 \\\n  --kv-transfer-config '{\"kv_connector\":\"HiSparseConnector\",\"kv_role\":\"kv_both\",\"kv_connector_extra_config\":{\"host_pool_gib\":64}}'\nvllm bench serve --model RedHatAI/GLM-5.3-NVFP4 --dataset-name random --random-input-len 20480 \\\n  --random-output-len 1024 --ignore-eos --seed 42 --max-concurrency 1 --num-prompts 4\nvllm bench serve --model RedHatAI/GLM-5.3-NVFP4 --dataset-name random --random-input-len 20480 \\\n  --random-output-len 1024 --ignore-eos --seed 42 --max-concurrency 4 --num-prompts 8\n```\n\nBecause of the fixed seed, the second wave repeats the first wave's prompts, so its requests hit the published prefix and adopt the GPU copies on admission.\n\n| | c=1 (4 prompts) | c=4 (8 prompts) |\n|---|---|---|\n| main `528772a4bf` (TP4 3/3 runs, TP8 4/4 runs) | 4/4 | 0/8: illegal memory access, engine dead |\n| this PR (TP4, 3 servers × 3 c=4 waves) | 4/4 | 8/8 in every wave, no CUDA errors (9/9 waves) |\n\n## Performance\n\nNo change expected: one dict pop per newly scheduled request per step, and one fewer row write on the GPU for adopted requests.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Repro above: fails on main (TP4 3/3, TP8 4/4), passes with this PR (9/9 c=4 waves over 3 TP4 servers), B200.\n- [x] Unit test `test_scheduled_prefix_hit_publishes_adopted_copies` now asserts the adopted row arrives in the new request's `block_ids` with no `block_table_updates` entry for it. Fails without the fix (`block_table_updates` still holds the request's row), passes with it.\n- [x] B200, 1 GPU:\n  - `pytest tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_hisparse_connector.py`: 8 passed\n  - `pytest tests/v1/e2e/general/test_hisparse.py`: 4 passed\n  - `pytest tests/v1/attention/test_sparse_mla_backends.py -k hisparse`: 36 passed\n\nNot a duplicate: no open PR touches this path. AI-assisted (Claude).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
